  "label": "User projected onto the messenger metaphor",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the 'messenger' role, as the text 'they can kill the messenger' implies a personal identification with the figure being persecuted. The visual of Jesus Christ on the cross, as the 'messenger', serves as a symbolic anchor for this projection, inviting the user to see themselves as a bearer of an unkillable message.",
